const definitions={
D001:row("Extended diameter is the supremum of extended pairwise distances, with empty diameter zero. Its real-valued interpretation is restricted to bounded Euclidean sets; no boundedness or existence assumption is introduced.",["spec.json#/definitions/0"]),
D002:row("The countable-cover infimum and positive-scale supremum specify unnormalized H with values in [0,infinity], positive exponent/scale, diameter bound ≤delta, and zero empty-member cost. These match problem.md:34-47. The stated usual-dimension interpretation is justified through the exported bridge N001, not an extra premise granted by this definition.",["spec.json#/definitions/1","problem.md:34-47","nl0.json#/propositions/9"]),
D003:row("The designation μH[a]=Measure.hausdorffMeasure a agrees with the pinned definition mkMetric(r↦r^a), including arbitrary-subset outer-measure evaluation and zero empty-set cost. Borel structure, real exponent and extended powers are explicit. Read Hausdorff.lean:410-440,464-469,535-552; the countable-cover formula remains M001.",["spec.json#/definitions/2","signature-evidence.json#/M001/0/sources/M001","nl0.json#/propositions/3"]),
D004:row("The supremum over nonnegative finite exponents with μH[a](A)=infinity agrees with native dimH and its Borelized definition (HausdorffDimension.lean:94-112). Codomain and empty supremum are explicit; exponent zero adds only zero to dimension. Positive-exponent equivalence with the supplied H is exported by N001, preserving the problem's normalization.",["spec.json#/definitions/3","signature-evidence.json#/M002/0/sources/M002","nl0.json#/propositions/9","problem.md:34-47"]),
D005:row("I is exactly [0,1] in the usual Euclidean real line, as in the selected target.",["spec.json#/definitions/4","problem.md:21-30"]),
D006:row("F=E×I is a defined set for every declared E and n. The coordinate identification explicitly fixes Euclidean distance sqrt(||x-y||²+|t-u|²), including the singleton R^0 case. It imposes no extra hypothesis and does not silently substitute a maximum product metric.",["spec.json#/definitions/5","spec.json#/parameters","problem.md:21-30"]),
D007:row("D is initially the extended nonnegative value dim_H(E), so its construction needs no finiteness guard. Finiteness and the finite-real identification are supplied by N002 before the positive-D upper/lower bound consumers R004/R006; the D=0 branch already makes D finite. No theorem is smuggled into the abbreviation.",["spec.json#/definitions/6","nl0.json#/propositions/10","global-overview.json#/inference_edges/3","global-overview.json#/inference_edges/5","nl0.json#/propositions/15"]),
D008:row("λ specifies standard Lebesgue measure with its usual interval-length normalization, its restriction to I, and the nonnegative extended-valued integral. The declared Borel sets and measurable nonnegative functions suffice for this notation. This fixes the standard measure rather than adding an original H; uses of measure/integration facts require their own local assessment.",["spec.json#/definitions/7","problem.md:116-141","problem.md:156-163"]),
D009:row("The indicator is explicitly defined pointwise for any real subset J with values zero and one in the stated nonnegative codomains. Its construction requires no measurability; measurability in actual integrations is a separate local obligation.",["spec.json#/definitions/8"])
};
const sources={
M001:row("Compared the full actual native telescope and pinned source Hausdorff.lean:444,535-552 with the statement: arbitrary extended metric X, Borel measurable structure, every real a, arbitrary subset A, positive extended scales (including infinity), natural-indexed covers, diameter ≤r, and nonempty-guarded rpow costs all agree. No measurable-cover-set premise is omitted. Signature probe exited 0 under Lean 4.32.2 and Mathlib 905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c; theorem kind and only propext/Classical.choice/Quot.sound are recorded. Source SHA256 e9595bc1e1cd2977ba420d9506745e59fdba9cfd75e7445b869b3128ae197d51 matches the retained binding. The finite-positive-scale/H identification belongs to R001, not this source judgment.",["nl0.json#/propositions/3","signature-evidence.json#/M001/0","spec.json#/pins"]),
M002:row("Actual signature and pinned HausdorffDimension.lean:94-118 agree: [EMetricSpace X] [MeasurableSpace X] [BorelSpace X], arbitrary subset, d:NNReal, strict d<dimH, conclusion μH[d]=infinity. The NL statement retains the full domain and strict inequality, including d=0. Native probe exited 0, declaration is a theorem, and its recorded axioms are only propext/Classical.choice/Quot.sound. Mathlib commit matches spec; source SHA256 fdc61e7f179044cd714058f209b100e51b6f8af69aff295e3ee629ed45dcee31 agrees with the retained binding.",["nl0.json#/propositions/4","signature-evidence.json#/M002/0","spec.json#/pins"]),
M003:row("Actual signature and the same pinned source readback at HausdorffDimension.lean:107-135 agree: arbitrary Borel extended metric space/subset and nonnegative finite d; dimH<d implies μH[d]=0. No finiteness, measurability or positive-measure premise is dropped. Native probe exited 0, theorem kind and standard recorded axioms agree; commit matches spec and shared source SHA256 fdc61e7f179044cd714058f209b100e51b6f8af69aff295e3ee629ed45dcee31 matches the binding.",["nl0.json#/propositions/5","signature-evidence.json#/M003/0","spec.json#/pins"]),
M004:row("Actual signature and shared pinned HausdorffDimension.lean:107-124 agree: arbitrary Borel extended metric X/subset, nonnegative finite d, μH[d](A)≠infinity implies dimH(A)≤d. The statement retains the exact non-infinity premise rather than requiring zero. Native probe exited 0, theorem kind/standard recorded axioms and pinned commit agree; shared source SHA256 fdc61e7f179044cd714058f209b100e51b6f8af69aff295e3ee629ed45dcee31 matches the binding.",["nl0.json#/propositions/6","signature-evidence.json#/M004/0","spec.json#/pins"]),
M005:row("Actual signature and shared pinned HausdorffDimension.lean:107-128 agree: arbitrary Borel extended metric X/subset, nonnegative finite d, μH[d](A)=infinity implies d≤dimH(A). There is no omitted positivity or nonemptiness premise. Native probe exited 0, theorem kind/standard recorded axioms and pinned commit agree; shared source SHA256 fdc61e7f179044cd714058f209b100e51b6f8af69aff295e3ee629ed45dcee31 matches the binding.",["nl0.json#/propositions/7","signature-evidence.json#/M005/0","spec.json#/pins"]),
M006:row("Actual signature and pinned Lebesgue/Add.lean:23-27,360-372 agree: arbitrary measurable α and measure μ, countable β, ENNReal-valued family with each member AEMeasurable; integral of the pointwise tsum equals tsum of integrals. Infinity is allowed; no finite-integral, probability or sigma-finiteness assumption is needed. Native probe exited 0, theorem kind and only standard recorded axioms agree; commit matches spec, and source SHA256 14da3dd3c2692219eec43e91c6b22bb02d5db7f00e03c789661c72dffecf7b4a matches the binding. Application measurability belongs to R005.",["nl0.json#/propositions/8","signature-evidence.json#/M006/0","spec.json#/pins"])
};
