structure_review:row("Canonical inputs/outputs agree with the exhaustive overview and spec hash binding. The AND edges are R001:(M001-M005)→N001; R002:(H001,H002,H003,N001)→N002; R003:N001→N003; R004:(N001,N002,N003)→N004; R005:(N002,M006)→N005; R006:(N001,N002,N005)→N006; R007:(H002,N001,N003)→N007; R008:(N002,N004,N006,N007)→P. Every N/P has exactly one producer, the listed order is topological, and all propositions are reachable from P. Roots are exactly H001-H003 and M001-M006; no internal result is a new assumption. All nine D dependencies are acyclic and definitions add no original H or desired conclusion. Exported statements identify their domains, exponents, scales, metric, extended values and branch conditions independently of producer bodies: N001 states the normalization bridge; N002 supplies finiteness and n=0; N003 states the interval facts; N005 states the all-positive-s,delta slicing inequality; N004/N006/N007 give complete bounds with explicit D branches. No private local witness escapes in these statements. Global graph consistency does not assert validity of any unreviewed local implication or actual prose dependency use.",["global-overview.json#/canonical_hashes","nl0.json#/spec_sha256","spec.json#/hypotheses","spec.json#/definitions","nl0.json#/propositions","global-overview.json#/inference_edges","nl0.json#/inferences/0/inputs","nl0.json#/inferences/0/output","nl0.json#/inferences/1/inputs","nl0.json#/inferences/1/output","nl0.json#/inferences/2/inputs","nl0.json#/inferences/2/output","nl0.json#/inferences/3/inputs","nl0.json#/inferences/3/output","nl0.json#/inferences/4/inputs","nl0.json#/inferences/4/output","nl0.json#/inferences/5/inputs","nl0.json#/inferences/5/output","nl0.json#/inferences/6/inputs","nl0.json#/inferences/6/output","nl0.json#/inferences/7/inputs","nl0.json#/inferences/7/output"]),
